this German group has been touring Iran  for one week they're just about to  return home the country's pulsating  capital of Tehran was the high point for  most of them their itinerary includes  museums and the Grand Bazaar which they  already knew from photos but their  personal contacts with the local people  proved to be quite different from what  they had expected  to tithe soup I denied the people were  really super very polite and courteous  they were always asking me where I come  from and offered me tea it was much more  than I had expected people at home are  astonished when you say you're going to  Iran they can't believe you can just go  there but once you're here you get  settled in right away so it's quite  normal to immediately start getting  around but they have to observe the  Islamic dress code and they're only  allowed to travel in a group not on  their own Tehran population 15 million  is a modern metropolis many Iranians  think tourism is their country's  greatest opportunity now that the  international isolation is ending and  plenty of people hope it will prove to  be a personal source of income Iran has  lots of well-educated young people but  unemployment is enormous Raisa Dennis  wah works in tourism specializing in  taking care of German tour groups  he knows Germany and speaks the language  fluently this year more than 5 million  foreign tourists visited Iran 25 percent  more than last year  if tourism continues to go well of  course there will be good opportunities  for those who want to work in this  industry and I could imagine there will  be jobs not only in the restaurant trade  but also in travel agencies and as tour  guides and so on that's a very important  positive factor in order to reduce  unemployment but Iran needs more modern  Western standard hotels the pent-up  demand is enormous Raisa fields plenty  of complaints and discusses them with  tour guides  the German group visits the golestan  palace at the end of its tour of Tehran  formerly it was the seat of government  for the Shah now it's a museum the  Germans were pleased with their visit to  Iran and can't wait to tell their  friends and families all about it
 

